<title>USA: Mutual Savings gets assessment exemption.</title>
<headline>Mutual Savings gets assessment exemption.</headline>
<dateline>BAY CITY, Mich. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mutual Savings Bank fsb said on Friday that it received an exemption from the one-time assessment to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund, but will instead pay semi-annual assessments through the end of 1999.</p>
<p>Mutual Savings estimated the total benefit to paying semi-annual assessments rather than the one-time payment would be about $1.9 million, based on its current risk classification.</p>
<p>Earlier on Friday, Mutual Savings reported net income of $314,000, or $0.07 a share, compared with a loss of $112,000, or $0.03 a share a year ago.</p>
<p>Shares of Mutal Savings closed unchanged at 5-1/4 on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
